  "purpose": "H.STA.BLK.1.2 HC Sinkhorn tail child FALLBACK k6b (hard child x2 in the HC root, TAILC=1): same netlist as k6; clock = pre-placed symmetric equal-delay spine (OT_SPINE_SYM 1, LEAF_N 16) from a clk pin at the S-face centre (k4b form). TPIPE 1 + SKP 3 (SQO + SC2) + SDIV 17, gate-level CLONED netlist (per-module ABC map, const-identity fold, bound_fanout_clone --limit 24, retained re-synth, compact). Square 388.8 x 388.8; mixes W / bases+scales+launch N / result E, clk+rst_n S. | SAFE checklist (HBMc/HC-TAIL 10-22, rebuilt after the k4 CTS: own TT STA 833.333 propagated WNS -177 / TNS -142k / 1,175 endpoints, 1,146 Sinkhorn: step-0 B quotient Q2 cone ~1,000 x -177..-96, A-step flt -156, steady st-decode-led P/Q1 -44/-31; tail exp add -55 = no added cycles (10-22 freeze): repair upsizing at route, LVT on <=~2% cells if still a near miss, NEXT-RELEASE only if TT < 0 after that): 1 pins PASS (RTL pin flop + 2nd stage on every data pin, output pin flops; rst_n reset_landing 2 then ot_rst_relay 3 regions + kept leaf) | 2 reach PASS 388.8 < 405, every pin->core hop registered | 3 fanout PASS clone limit 24 + pre-floorplan native census in gate | 4 depth FIXED inside the accepted latency: ot_hdc_sinkhorn_cp SC2 = QS cut in the step-0 B quotients (D_B 10->11; standalone TT Q2 -911 -> -97 unrepaired, fanout-only), A-step normalise/a_bad cut (D_A 7->8), decoded state registers sd_e/sd_m/sd_z (steady P/Q1 start at registers); steady D 16 unchanged, no MCP | 5 storage PASS no array > 2 kb (mix store = root SRAM) | 6 floorplan PASS util ~0.35-0.41 (k4 CTS 41%), no macros, square | 7 clock one root clk, no derived clock; boundary pin-flop spread <= 80 by --cts gate | 8 reset PASS control/valid only, regional relay. Schedule static: L 989 (TR 271 + SDIV 17 + CAP 699 + 2) + OPIPE 1 output pin stage = result_v at launch + 992 (child offset over the unit 496; root TSKP 3 / TSDIV 17, compiler --tail-x 494, TE 2). | HBMc/HC-TAIL2 10-22: k4b route NEEDS_RTL core -> result -487 (252 of 770 output ports not pin-anchored: final_result is a hold-mux register) -> OPIPE 1 dedicated output pin flops; native netlist regenerated with yosys 0.68 (yosys 0.52 dfflibmap swapped ASAP7 async set/clear: every async reset inverted in k3..k5 natives, the k5 native 5/48).",
